{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tasty-unappeased-leopard","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# A gate run does not notice its own binary is older than the base ref it pins\n\n`review-plan` snapshots the base ref's config into\n`/tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots/<sha>/rebar.toml` and reviews against it, but nothing compares\nthe RUNNING BUILD to that sha. A checkout that has drifted behind `origin/main` silently\nreviews new material with old code.\n\n## Observed\nThree consecutive `review-plan` runs were executed from `~/rebar/.venv` — a legitimate repo\ncheckout venv, which is what AGENTS.md asks for — while that checkout sat 24 commits behind\n`origin/main`. The only symptom was one easily-missed line:\n\n    WARNING rebar.config: rebar config (/tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots/2bce1407.../rebar.toml):\n    unknown key 'verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets' ignored (typo? see docs/config.md)\n\nThat key is not a typo. Commit 74a7332606 (\"9416: rename overlap_enabled for what it does\")\nrenamed `verify.overlap_enabled` -> `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets` and added the alias\n`_ALIASES = {\"verify\": {\"overlap_enabled\": \"suggest_duplicate_tickets\"}}`. The stale build\npredates the rename, so it read the CURRENT base ref's config, did not recognise the current\nkey name, and silently fell back to a default.\n\n## Why it is worth a guard rather than a doc line\nThe cost was not the config key; it was ~15 minutes of wall time per review. The same commit\nrange contains 7fa8102477 (\"Bound malformed overlap judge calls\"). On the stale build the\noverlap judge failed on EVERY batch:\n\n    llm call [overlap-judge] mode=single_turn FAILED in 310.0s: Exceeded maximum output retries (2)\n    overlap judge batch call failed; treating as abstain\n\n~310s per batch, three batches observed, each ending in `abstain` — so the review paid full\nlatency for a step that contributed nothing, and the failure was non-fatal and therefore\ninvisible in the verdict. AGENTS.md already warns \"VERIFY THE BINARY, NOT THE SOURCE TREE\"\nabout the pipx global install; this is the sibling trap, where the binary IS a repo build and\nstill wrong.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] When the running build's commit is not an ancestor-or-equal of the base ref a gate pins,\n      the gate emits a single prominent warning naming both shas and the drift count. It does\n      NOT fail — reviewing from a slightly-behind checkout is legitimate — but it stops being\n      silent.\n- [ ] An unknown key in a config snapshot the gate itself produced is reported differently\n      from a user typo: 'unknown key X (this build may predate it)' when the build is behind\n      the pinned ref, since 'typo?' actively misdirects.\n- [ ] Held-out test: a gate run whose build is behind the pinned base ref emits the drift\n      warning; a run at/ahead of it does not.\n- [ ] Consider surfacing repeated non-fatal LLM step failures in the run summary. Three\n      310-second `abstain`s produced no signal a caller would see.\n\n## Provenance\nFound while re-running plan review for task b2bb during the store/signing remediation.\nRe-running from a worktree venv at origin/main is the workaround.","id":"b273-e0ba-f719-4f1c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gate runs do not warn when the running build is behind the base ref"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786383846571877001,"uuid":"2334686a-e711-4e8e-bec0-b35f4e73ff4c"}